lkova D","lastName":"Mikhalkova","firstName":"Deana","initials":"D"},{"fullName":"Fitzgerald K","lastName":"Fitzgerald","firstName":"Kathleen","initials":"K"},{"fullName":"Whellan DJ","lastName":"Whellan","firstName":"David J","initials":"DJ"},{"fullName":"Wever-Pinzon O","lastName":"Wever-Pinzon","firstName":"Omar","initials":"O"},{"fullName":"Gutierrez J","lastName":"Gutierrez","firstName":"Jonathan","initials":"J"},{"fullName":"Goldsborough Y","lastName":"Goldsborough","firstName":"Yavette","initials":"Y"},{"fullName":"Gilotra NA","lastName":"Gilotra","firstName":"Nisha A","initials":"NA"},{"fullName":"Caikauskaite I","lastName":"Caikauskaite","firstName":"Indre","initials":"I"},{"fullName":"Skopicki HA","lastName":"Skopicki","firstName":"Hal A","initials":"HA"},{"fullName":"Huggins GS","lastName":"Huggins","firstName":"Gordon S","initials":"GS"},{"fullName":"Yuen N","lastName":"Yuen","firstName":"Nathan","initials":"N"},{"fullName":"Haynes A","lastName":"Haynes","firstName":"Abbey","initials":"A"},{"fullName":"Katie C","lastName":"Katie","firstName":"Carr","initials":"C"},{"fullName":"Snell G","lastName":"Snell","firstName":"Gail","initials":"G"},{"fullName":"Smith AL","lastName":"Smith","firstName":"Andrew L","initials":"AL"},{"fullName":"Walker B","lastName":"Walker","firstName":"Brandon","initials":"B"},{"fullName":"Johnson J","lastName":"Johnson","firstName":"Jovita","initials":"J"},{"fullName":"Henderson S","lastName":"Henderson","firstName":"Simmone","initials":"S"},{"fullName":"Pauwaa S","lastName":"Pauwaa","firstName":"Sunil","initials":"S"},{"fullName":"Bhat G","lastName":"Bhat","firstName":"Geetha","initials":"G"},{"fullName":"Gagliardi A","lastName":"Gagliardi","firstName":"Ann","initials":"A"}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-8175-168X"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-8409-8030"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-5931-1239"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9630-7204"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"1","volume":"7","journalIssueId":3293263,"dateOfPublication":"2022 Jan","monthOfPublication":1,"yearOfPublication":2022,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"JAMA Cardiol","title":"JAMA cardiology","essn":"2380-6591","issn":"2380-6583","isoabbreviation":"JAMA Cardiol","nlmid":"101676033"},"printPublicationDate":"2022-01-01"},"pubYear":"2022","pageInfo":"17-25","abstractText":"<h4>Importance</h4>The use of sacubitril/valsartan is not endorsed by practice guidelines for use in patients with New York Heart Association class IV heart failure with a reduced ejection fraction because of limited clinical experience in this population.<h4>Objective</h4>To compare treatment with sacubitril/valsartan treatment with valsartan in patients with advanced heart failure and a reduced ejection fraction and recent New York Heart Association class IV symptoms.<h4>Design, setting, and participants</h4>A double-blind randomized clinical trial was conducted; a total of 335 patients with advanced heart failure were included. The trial began on March 2, 2017, and was stopped early on March 23, 2020, owing to COVID-19 risk.<h4>Intervention</h4>Patients were randomized to receive sacubitril/valsartan (target dose, 200 mg twice daily) or valsartan (target dose, 160 mg twice daily) in addition to recommended therapy.<h4>Main outcomes and measures</h4>The area under the curve (AUC) for the ratio of N-terminal pro-brain natriuretic peptide (NT-proBNP) compared with baseline measured through 24 weeks of therapy.<h4>Results</h4>Of the 335 patients included in the analysis, 245 were men (73%); mean (SD) age was 59.4 (13.5) years. Seventy-two eligible patients (18%) were not able to tolerate sacubitril/valsartan, 100 mg/d, during the short run-in period, and 49 patients (29%) discontinued sacubitril/valsartan during the 24 weeks of the trial. The median NT-proBNP AUC for the valsartan treatment arm (n = 168) was 1.19 (IQR, 0.91-1.64), whereas the AUC for the sacubitril/valsartan treatment arm (n = 167) was 1.08 (IQR, 0.75-1.60). The estimated ratio of change in the NT-proBNP AUC was 0.95 (95% CI 0.84-1.08; P = .45). Compared with valsartan, treatment with sacubitril/valsartan did not improve the clinical composite of number of days alive, out of hospital, and free from heart failure events. Aside from a statistically significant increase in non-life-threatening hyperkalemia in the sacubitril/valsartan arm (28 [17%] vs 15 [9%]; P = .04), there were no observed safety concerns.<h4>Conclusions and relevance</h4>The findings of this trial showed that, in patients with chronic advanced heart failure with a reduced ejection fraction, there was no statistically significant difference between sacubitril/valsartan and valsartan with respect to reducing NT-proBNP levels.<h4>Trial registration</h4>ClinicalTrials.gov Identifier: NCT02816736.","affiliation":"Department of Medicine, Washington University in St Louis, St Louis, Missouri.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Randomized Controlled Trial","Journal Article","Research Support, N.I.H., Extramural"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"NHLBI NIH HHS","acronym":"HL","grantId":"U10 HL110302","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NHLBI NIH HHS","acronym":"HL","grantId":"U01 HL084904","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NHLBI NIH HHS","acronym":"HL","grantId":"U10 HL110262","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NHLBI NIH HHS","acronym":"HL","grantId":"U10 HL110309","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NHLBI NIH HHS","acronym":"HL","grantId":"U10 HL110297","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NHLBI NIH HHS","acronym":"HL","grantId":"U10 HL110336","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NHLBI NIH HHS","acronym":"HL","grantId":"U10 HL110338","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NHLBI NIH HHS","acronym":"HL","grantId":"U10 HL110342","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NHLBI NIH HHS","acronym":"HL","grantId":"U10 HL110337","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NHLBI NIH HHS","acronym":"HL","grantId":"U10 HL110312","order